        "answer": {
          "short": "$x\\approx9.71\\text{ m}$. Student B is more accurate. Student A rounded $\\sin31^\\circ$ too early.",
          "worked": "The $5\\text{ m}$ side is opposite $31^\\circ$, and $x$ is the hypotenuse.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin31^\\circ&=\\frac{5}{x}\\\\x\\sin31^\\circ&=5\\\\x&=\\frac{5}{\\sin31^\\circ}\\\\x&\\approx9.71\\text{ m}\\end{align*}$$\nStudent B is more accurate. Student A rounded $\\sin31^\\circ$ to $0.52$ before dividing. Keep the calculator's full precision until the final answer.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
